Z||000008||wkayl||12-30-2001||10:19 PM||||I have a Nextel for work.  I believe the 2-way only works in the region you reside.  Here in Colorado I think we can talk as far as Salt Lake City, but I may be mistaken (I never tried it).||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||12-31-2001||09:12 AM||||I have a Southern LINC phone. Technology is identical to Nextel. <BR>The two way thing only works if both units are programmed with the same <I>fleet</I> code, or are cross-fleet capable. (Only the newer units do this.) It's still just a one-on-one call. No party line, unless both units are on the same talkgroup within the fleet. Highly unlikely that any two units are even on the same fleet, unless they are ordered that way.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
